WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.460
How Israel influences British politics-

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.680
We reveal from the inside how the Israeli Embassy

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.820
penetrates different levels of British democracy in the first of four programmes:

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.980
The Battle for Britain's Youth

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.820
[sounds of explosions and yelling]

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.440
Following decades of violence

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.960
a new challenge has emerged to Israel's occupation of Palestinian lands called BDS.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.620
[crowd chants] "BDS is here to stay"

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.760
That's the global movement to boycott, divest,
and impose sanctions on Israel,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.720
and expose it as an apartheid state.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.240
The Israeli Government has responded with a campaign to rebrand the country's image.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.580
[Israeli Prime Minister, Benjamin Netanyahu] "The reason we should fight BDS is because it's wrong. It's a moral outrage."

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.140
It's an operation run by the secretive
Ministry of Strategic Affairs.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.940
"They recruit mainly former intelligence officers."

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.220
"Its main task is to counter BDS worldwide."

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:07.920
Using an undercover reporter, Al Jazeera's investigative unit exposes Israel's clandestine activities in London,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.540
a city that's  become a major battleground.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.660
"BDS campaign in many ways germinated in Britain."

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.000
You'll meet the people working to challenge 
BDS at every level of British  politics.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.160
One of Israel's main targets is the Labour party.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.300
For the first time its leader
is a champion of Palestinian civil rights.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.900
They'd be very happy to see Jeremy Corbyn no longer leader of the Labour party for sure.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:42.300
It's a covert action that penetrates
the heart of Britain's democracy.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.200
It is outrageous interference in British politics, 
it shouldn't be permitted.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:56.300
It's a battle of ideas seeking to change not only how Israel's portrayed, but even how it is debated.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:16.080
Our undercover reporter grew up in Germany and creates an identity as a graduate planning to live in Britain.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:24.360
Robin sets himself up in London as an aspiring Labour party activist with strong sympathies toward Israel.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.920
After over a month of attending party functions, 
he stood out as a friend of Israel.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.100
And before long, he recognized a familiar face.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.400
It's a meeting of the Labour Friends of Israel or LFI,

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.640
- members of the British Parliament, who lobby for Israel.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.800
Oh yeah, take the districts

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.940
Shai later explained to Robin
the problems the LFI is facing.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.960
Robin tweeted and wrote articles about Israel and the Labour party, building up his online identity.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.440
He discovered numerous groups that support Israel  -

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:05.540
- and which identify themselves as
 independent grassroots movements.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.140
One is the Sussex Friends Of Israel -

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:15.040
- who organized a march to protest against 
the pro-Palestinian movement to boycott Israel.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.980
Robin had joined them.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.800
Shai later described the embassy's role
 in  some of these movements.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.120
Shai had helped establish a youth group 
within the Conservative Friends of Israel.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.340
Alright, thank you very much

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.600
Have a nice evening, right

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.880
Our investigation linked the embassy's senior political officer with a series of pro-Israel groups -

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:22.940
- the parliamentary friends of Israel, young conservatives, lobbyists,

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.500
as well as grassroots movements.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.280
In addition, Shai's involved with the
youth arm of the Fabian Society -

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.600
- an influential Labour party think tank.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:08.880
It appears the Israeli diplomat's' mission is to build support for Israel at all levels of the Labour party.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.060
Shai says he knows nearly all
the Fabian Society activists.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:52.520
Martin Edobor explains how foreign governments' support helps the Fabian membership.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:14.200
I went on one of the trips of the Conservative
Friends of Israel to the Middle East.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.640
It was brilliantly well arranged, very well looked after.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.060
You got fantastic access. You did meet Palestinians.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:26.660
If all you did was rely on that one trip,            
you would get a very one-sided point of view.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:45.380
According to Haaretz newspaper, Israel, which controls all water sources in the Occupied West Bank,

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.140
- did cut supplies, even if the reason was contested.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Our undercover reporter discovered that Shai Masot     
played a role in another key Labour party organization -

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.440
- The Jewish Labour Movement, or JLM.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.020
Robin attended a summer 
barbecue organized by the JLM.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.700
Much of the small talk turned to the Israeli embassy.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.280
What came next surprised our undercover reporter.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:19.700
Shai had asked Robin to become part of the Israeli        
Embassy's plan to attract young Labour party members.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:54.400
Shai then suggested that as well as setting up the Young LFI, Robin apply for a job at the Israeli embassy.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.260
He was invited to a private meeting at a London hotel.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:05.740
It included embassy staff
and British supporters of Israel.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.840
An Israeli diplomat takes Robin to one side.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.300
Ella Rose, the new director of the Jewish Labour Movement, was pleased to hear -

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.100
- of Robin's plans to set up a Young LFI.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.940
The guest of honour: a minister
from the Israeli government.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:26.600
The primary role of Israel's Strategic Affairs Ministry
is to counter the BDS movement.

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:55.980
During another meeting with the
embassy's senior political officer,

00:13:56.340 --> 00:14:00.220
Shai tutors Robin on setting up a new pro-Israel group.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:29.820
The LFI appears to be looking 
beyond Labour's present set of MPs.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:50.960
Robin tells him about the Israeli 
Embassy's interest in recruiting him.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:04.120
He gave an example of how a job at the embassy  
could  further a career in British politics.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.280
Round about the same time the JLM -

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:47.560
- re-emerged under the leadership of Jeremy Newmark,

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:52.100
- who would later hire Ella Rose
as the  director of the JLM.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:56.780
The big story was about a young student
in Oxford, who made allegations -

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:01.420
- that  the Labour party and most of the student left at Oxford  was anti-Semitic.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.140
He didn't present any evidence at all. 
The only thing he said was -

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:07.420
- that they had promoted the Israel Apartheid Week,

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:11.700
- which is a well-known event which takes 
place on campuses around the world.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:15.840
The national chairman of  Labour Students
at that time was Michael Rubin.

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.700
There was lots of media leaks and talks about

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:36.220
how anti-Semitism was being covered up.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:43.200
British newspapers repeatedly ran stories of 
anti-Semitism in the Labour party.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:50.740
One of the next targets was Malia Bouattia, the newly elected leader of Britain's National Union of Students.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.620
Palestine, Palestine.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:30.980
With each year of Israel's expanding occupation, 
support for BDS has spread  -

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.640
- on college campuses around the world.

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:40.860
In Britain, the Israeli-Palestinian conflict defined the 2016 election for the NUS presidency.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:45.940
But Israel, where it exists now, 
is that problematic to you?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:51.320
Israel as it behaves, is problematic to me.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:55.720
You would feel it would be O.K. for you to say about yourself that you are anti-Zionist?

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.460
Yes, I would.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:29.540
Another vice president, Richard Brooks, took the unusual step of publicly claiming that Bouttia's criticisms -

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.880
- of Israel amount to anti-Semitism.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:52.820
When you look at what Malia Bouttia has been saying - she says... it's... her criticisms are political ones.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.920
She talks about Zionism, 
not about people who are Jewish.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:21:00.500
Yeah, I think that the really important thing here, and something that student movement needs to face up to,

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:05.420
is that it is for Jewish students to find what anti-Semitism is in the run up to national conference.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:10.820
Nearly 50 union of Jewish  student presidents of societies made it clear that they had concerns about some of the rhetoric.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:13.800
Brooks never mentioned 
that weeks before that interview,

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:18.520
- he'd been taken to Israel as part of a 
delegation from the Union of Jewish Students.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:22:01.080
During the runup to the election, Richard Brooks had held private meetings with Russell Langer,

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.380
the campaign director of the Union of Jewish  Students.

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:08.300
Also attending the meetings was Michael Rubin.

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:29.360
After being introduced by the Israeli Embassy
as a Young LFI volunteer,

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:35.060
- our undercover reporter explores the possibility of ousting the pro-Palestinian NUS president -

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:37.120
- with the help of Richard Brooks.

00:22:55.100 --> 00:23:02.560
Our investigation also revealed that the UJS,          
who sent critics of Malia Bouttia on trips to Israel,

00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:06.320
- has received money from the Israeli Embassy.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:35.240
In 2016, Schapira launched an unsuccessful bid 
for the presidency of the UJS.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.740
He also received donations from Israel to set up a new campus-based think tank.

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:45.480
He established a Pinsker Centre with former 
University College student Elliot Miller.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:18.020
They also confirmed for the first time that the powerful American pro-Israel lobby, AIPAC,

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:22.420
- is channelling money to British campuses
through the Pinsker Centre.

00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:33.620
Elliot Miller remains vocal in the cauldron
of London student politics.

00:25:28.600 --> 00:25:33.840
In episode two: further evidence of Israel's involvement in Britain's Labour party.

00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:42.400
And the money Israel gives
Labour MPs to help improve its image.

